{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1792715468341084944,"compiled_state":{"alias":"young-snaky-monkfish","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":1},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f789271b1be3d93e5d465e640a31cb7a50434cc68afc870dc943864aa67791d0","event_uuid":"c3ff11b2-a400-4c56-8a38-ed2a4916d16d","position":{"commit_sha":"e0e8a0cf7b5ef466682a48aa9e9780772f81cb03","position":"1792699926150068460-c3ff11b2-a400-4c56-8a38-ed2a4916d16d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1792699926150068460,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d11a05ab-b486-4d31-93bd-42f420ae9600","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ad8a-38e7-44d3-4662"}],"description":"## Observation\n`batch_dispatch.reroute_migrated_plans` (`src/rebar/reconciler/batch_dispatch.py:688-745` on origin/main dcb35ce77fe) selects a plan as migrated when every mutation's action is in `NON_CREATE_FAMILIES` and routes to the coordinator. It never checks direction. Its sibling `_ordered_create_plans` (`:395-406`) does check `direction == \"outbound\"`.\n\n`run_differs` plans every typed mutation, inbound and outbound (`run_differs.py:299-313`), and `apply_phase` passes those plans to `applier.apply`. So an inbound `update`, `conflict` or `repair_property` plan qualifies, and `run_migrated_reroute` dispatches it through `make_coordinator_dispatch` → `apply_handlers.dispatch_mutation`, the outbound handlers.\n\nReproduction: fake transport, real `applier.apply`, plans from `ticket_planner.plan_pass`. The probe is `inbound_probe/apply_e2e.py` in the `lane-ebf5` scratch directory.\n- With 1 inbound update for DIG-1 (payload `fields` plus 1 Jira comment) and 1 outbound update for DIG-2, the transport receives `update_issue('DIG-1')`, `add_comment('DIG-1', 'jira comment')` and `update_issue('DIG-2')`. The Jira-side change is written back to Jira, and the Jira comment is posted to Jira again.\n- With the inbound update alone, the transport receives no calls, because `_apply_batch` is not reached when there are no outbound dicts.\n- Same result at f5f666702b4. The selection filter has been unchanged since d49466b5e96 (2026-08-25, \"Wire live coordinator+fuse non-create reroute\").\n\nUnverified: a live pass. The fake transport accepts every call, so whether the real outbound comment path deduplicates against existing Jira comments has not been checked.\n\n## Hypotheses\n- (a) Live passes that contain both inbound updates and any outbound mutation echo the inbound field values and comments back to Jira, possibly creating duplicate Jira comments.\n- (b) A later guard in the real transport or the outbound comment handler suppresses the echo, so the defect is latent.\n\nThese remain unproven.\n\n## Approach\n1. Add a regression test that reproduces the probe: an inbound update plus an outbound update through `applier.apply` with plans from `plan_pass`. It asserts the transport receives no write for the inbound target.\n2. Restrict `reroute_migrated_plans` to plans whose mutations are all `outbound`, matching `_ordered_create_plans`. Inbound mutations keep dispatching through `_apply_typed`.\n3. Check the live bridge-run history and Jira for duplicate comments on issues that had inbound comment syncs since 2026-08-25. This tests hypothesis (a).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The regression test fails on dcb35ce77fe and passes with the fix.\n- [ ] `reroute_migrated_plans` selects only all-outbound plans; a unit test covers inbound update, conflict and repair_property plans.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The live check result for hypothesis (a) is recorded on this ticket.\n  provenance: environment=production Jira; principal=bridge bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — issue keys and comment ids recorded on the ticket","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b594-de6d-3ebc-490f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Coordinator reroute dispatches inbound update plans through the outbound handlers","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c3ff11b2-a400-4c56-8a38-ed2a4916d16d","d11a05ab-b486-4d31-93bd-42f420ae9600"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792715468341084944,"uuid":"a0469360-4f08-4bf6-953a-fb7c4f8a857a"}